WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.520
Neo Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:06.060
Ultimate Photon Stream!!

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:13.030
III!!

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.660
IV, are you ready for your punishment?!

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.990
Ultimate Photon Stream!!

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.020
You did it, Kaito!

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.400
Yuma won!

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.690
Kaito-<i>sama</i>!

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.660
Impossible... For me to...

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.660
For me to lose...!

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.370
Kaito!

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.130
Hey, Kaito!

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.380
Kaito-<i>sama</i>!

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.550
Haruto... Where is Haruto?

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.100
Where is he?!

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.560
Hell if I know that.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:29.350
Then I'll just ask your rotten souls <i>directly</i>!

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:38.910
What?!

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.800
<i>I can't retrieve their Numbers!</i>

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.800
Wh-What the?

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:03.850
That's...

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:07.100
Astral!

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:08.850
I'm fine.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:10.850
Pointless.

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:14.530
We're protected by these crests.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.070
Remember that!

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:21.320
We'll give you back the pain you gave us double!

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:22.660
Wh-What the?

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.450
H-He disappeared!

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:29.410
Yuma Tsukumo...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:30.960
III...

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.550
Let's go home now.

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:37.260
Wait!

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:39.930
Where is Haruto?!

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:42.260
Give Haruto back!

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:54.190
They both... disappeared.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.320
Haruto...

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:01.780
Haruto is right up here.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.120
Haruto!

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.960
You're...!

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:20.920
You're the guy from before!

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.890
<i>I will grant Haruto-</i>sama<i>'s wish.</i>

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.100
<i>Hey, hold up a minute!</i>

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.510
<i>Let's go.</i>

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:30.180
- How dare you... How dare you trick-
 - Move!

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.520
Why?! Why are you...?!

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:40.610
Haruto!

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:54.630
Haruto...

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.710
Haruto-<i>sama</i>!

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.670
What did... What did you do to Haruto?!

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:05.050
Do not worry. He is still alive.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.970
But he used up all of his power.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:12.520
Yes, he gave the remainder of his power to you.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:13.520
What?

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.980
<i>This time I'll protect my brother!</i>

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:30.620
It can't be... I did this to Haruto?

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.620
What did you do to Haruto?!

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:39.800
Yuma Tsukumo... You are Kazuma-<i>san</i>'s son, right?

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.800
Huh? How do you know my dad?!

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.260
Your dad is alive.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.430
In the Astral World.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:54.080
<i>As I get closer, I stretch my hand out</i>

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:57.130
<i>towards that shining light leading towards tomorrow</i>

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:04.390
<i>I dream of a world that expands from my feet.</i>

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:13.650
<i>I haven't a clue of where things like dreams and hopes are at.</i>

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:18.150
<i>Even if I run looking for it, I still can't seem to find it.</i>

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:24.610
<i>I wonder if I have fallen into a gap of truth and lies.</i>

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:29.410
<i>Even so, our grand tale has yet to begin.</i>

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:35.080
<i>Let's move on towards tomorrow, 
even if our road begins to fall apart.</i>

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:40.340
<i>I will jump forward, before all my
 strength completely drains.</i>

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:43.220
<i>The closer I get, the further it becomes,</i>

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:46.510
<i>that truth that I must seize.</i>

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:51.680
<i>It's to find hope that we desire from a future unseen.</i>

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:54.270
<i>With a heart stronger than anyone else,</i>

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:57.440
<i>I'll learn to keep running up.</i>

00:05:57.770 --> 00:06:02.990
<i>With the strength to win any battle, 
despite just how weak I am,</i>

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:05.490
<i>My purpose is to find,</i>

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:08.490
<i>with these invaluable friends of mine,</i>

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:15.290
<i>The future of the world expanding
 from my feet with my own eyes.</i>

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:27.110
"Number 44: The Forked Paths of Destiny!
 Yuma Abandons Dueling!"

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:27.110
Dad... might still be alive?

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.570
<i>What do you mean by that?! Hey!</i>

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.620
<i>Dad... My dad's alive?!</i>

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.040
<i>Hey, wait up!</i>

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:45.170
<i>What do you mean that my father is in the Astral World?!</i>

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:48.260
<i>What do you mean by that?!</i>

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:55.640
Hey... Astral World's the place you come from, right?

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:58.890
Why would my dad be there?

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:00.020
I'm not sure...

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.770
My memories are...

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:07.780
Then if we collect the Numbers and get your memories back... then...

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:13.280
<i>Haruto... He's sick.</i>

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:19.210
<i>Kaito, you're a pitiful soldier working for Haruto's sake.</i>

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:23.710
<i>To save my brother, I sold my soul to the devil.</i>

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:26.170
Then...

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:28.460
Haruto... won't recover.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:33.340
But if Haruto gets better...

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:38.020
<i>My mission is to destroy the Astral World.</i>

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:42.020
And if my dad's really in Astral World...

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:45.190
God, I don't know!

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:48.360
What the heck should I do?!

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:54.120
That's right!

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:57.700
That's right! My dad might still be alive!

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:59.370
My dad!

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.000
Dad!

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.330
Y-Yuma!

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:21.350
Calm down!

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:23.480
This mood ain't like you!

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:25.940
Move.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.730
No can do. You can't take a single step beyond this point.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:32.150
I will protect Haruto.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:34.820
I won't let you guys do whatever you like with him!

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:36.200
Knock it off, Kaito.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:41.250
Even if you stand by Haruto's side, you can't do a thing.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.750
You have no choice but to leave this to Mr. Heartland for now.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:46.880
You know this.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:57.510
Kaito, why didn't you tell us that Yuma Tsukumo was working with the Original Number?

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.220
You know about that?

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:00.560
Pretty much.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.890
I'm the one hunting him.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:04.690
Funny you should say that.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:07.520
You got along well during that Tag Duel, didn't you?

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.400
You had a nice mood going and everything!

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:12.070
He's my prey.

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:13.860
I'm the one who will defeat him!

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:17.320
Everyone holding a Number is my enemy.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:23.000
If you stand before me as a hindrance, I'll consider you my enemy.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:33.260
Haruto! Oh, Haruto!

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:36.760
I'm sorry! I'm responsible for all of this!

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:38.260
Haruto!

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:42.140
Your grief and sadness is much appreciated, Faker-<i>sama</i>.

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:46.480
Mr. Heartland, who stole Haruto's power?!

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:51.900
According to Kaito's report, it was the doing of a group of people wielding special crests.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:53.940
Crests?

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:59.820
These people will eventually show themselves again during the Duel Carnival.

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:02.910
Very well. Let's take those people apart!

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:08.210
And we will take Haruto's power back from them!

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:09.750
With pleasure.

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:23.600
Yuma, are you serious?

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:24.140
Yeah!

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:30.770
I've got no choice but to go to Astral World and find my dad with my own two hands.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:34.230
Then the Numbers...

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:38.820
You don't care about the Numbers?

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:41.200
It's not like I don't care about them.

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:46.370
But Dad... Dad might be alive.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:54.300
That's why, for now I...

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:59.130
For now, you'll have to cut me some slack!

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:09.770
What's with that getup of yours?

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:11.650
Running away from home?

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:14.060
I am not running away from home!

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:15.730
Sis, don't get too surprised!

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:18.190
You're about to say Dad might still be alive, right?

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:19.110
Eh?

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:21.320
I heard about it from Kotori-<i>chan</i>.

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.740
So you're trying to find Dad and bring him home?

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:25.990
You're a true blue fool, you know that?

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.750
Dad said he found the top of the world, right?

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:34.040
Then I'll go to the top of the world and find Dad there!

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:35.790
Later!

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:37.050
Hold it, Yuma!

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:42.970
Whether it's the top of the world or the Astral World, I'm definitely gonna find you!

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.430
Wait for me, Dad!

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:47.470
If that's the case, what about the Duel Carnival?

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.060
The heck?

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.480
I'm right up here.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:59.190
Been some time, wouldn't ya say?

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:08.950
Grandpa Rokujuro!

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:15.670
Yuma, are you... abandoning Dueling?

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.050
No...

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:23.260
When I heard my cute little disciple was trying his best and standing up challenge after challenge,

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:25.260
I decided to leave the mountain.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:27.010
And here I am.

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:29.970
But I had no idea such a thing happened.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:32.270
I'm glad you understand!

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:33.810
Well then, I'm off.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:35.100
Hold your horses.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:35.690
Huh?

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:40.940
Yuma, wanna do this?

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:45.610
Sorry Gramps, but I don't really feel like Dueling right now...

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.080
I am your master!

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:50.830
You will not abandon Dueling that easily!

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:54.830
If you insist on leaving, you'll do it only after defeating me!

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.250
I understand.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:01.380
I accept!

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:06.840
I apologize Yuma, but I'm not going to help you out during this Duel.

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:09.140
Sure, I'll be able to handle this all on my own!

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.350
Come!

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.810
Let's go, Gramps!

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:22.820
Duel Disk, set!

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:27.530
D-Gazer, set!

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:34.330
<i>AR Vision - Link established.</i>

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:36.330
Duel!!

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:44.380
Haruto's power is beginning to awaken inside me.

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:09.700
My turn! Draw!

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.910
Yes! She's here!

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.830
I Summon Gagaga Girl!

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:28.510
Heck yeah! Now I've got five Monsters on my field!

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:32.180
Gramps only has one face-down Monster!

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:34.390
This turn will decide it!

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:41.900
Gagaga Girl, attack his face-down Monster!

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.940
Gagaga Formation!

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.320
Go on, everyone!

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:51.820
Trap Card, open!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:54.790
Holy Barrier - Mirror Force!

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:12.300
My Monsters were all... wiped out!

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:16.560
When fighting a match, you must <i>also</i> be sure to <i>notice</i> your opponent's set cards.

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:20.270
Hmph! But <i>I've </i>still got the advantage here!

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.600
Turn end!

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:24.820
Hm, then I guess it's my turn.

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:25.860
Draw.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:27.320
Hm, finally here.

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:30.700
I Flip Summon Queen's Knight!

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:40.040
Then I Normal Summon King's Knight!

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.630
King, Queen...

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:49.090
It can't be...

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:51.300
This ain't over yet!

00:15:51.300 --> 00:16:00.020
When both Queen and King Knight are on the field, I can play the Jack card on the field from my deck!

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:05.730
Come forth, Jack's Knight!

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:12.320
Three Monsters all at once!

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:13.860
I knew it...

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:16.580
It's a three-Monster-for-one combo.

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:20.160
And here we have this!

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:24.460
I activate the Fusion Magic Card from my hand!

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:28.000
I fuse together the three royal knights!

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:31.590
Come forth, Imperial Knight!

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:35.680
I Summon the ultimate Fusion warrior, Arcana Knight Joker!

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.310
3800 Attack Points!

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:40.310
You gotta be kidding me!

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:41.980
The tables have turned!

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:45.440
Go, Arcana Knight Joker!

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:48.400
Direct Attack Yuma!

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:58.120
Yuma!

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.540
Darn it! Let's play another round!

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:04.040
Guts!!

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:05.250
Huh?

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:07.830
Why are you in such a rush, Yuma?

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:10.710
As you are now, you couldn't even defeat <i>me</i>!

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:13.720
As you are now, you can't see a thing!

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:19.010
B-But... I just don't know what to do.

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:22.430
Do I choose Astral or Haruto?

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:25.560
I can't possibly decide something like that!

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:26.560
So...

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.520
You tried to run.

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:31.020
You planned to use searching for your father as an excuse.

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:33.030
I ran away...

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:36.990
Abandoning your rivals and your friends...

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:42.200
You abandoned your family and even your partner.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:45.660
Your partner must feel the same.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:49.170
Yuma, look at your feet carefully.

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:52.840
Your feet are strongly rooted in Dueling.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:55.800
So use Dueling as your guide.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:58.590
And take your first step from there toward your goal.

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:02.140
Your father is certain to be there.

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:07.230
Because Dueling is the bond that connects you to him!

00:18:07.230 --> 00:18:08.770
Gramps...

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.690
I... I...

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:14.360
I really do love Dueling!

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:15.610
I love it!

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:32.130
Incredible! This is incredible!

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:39.380
I can't believe it's so difficult to gain control over it, even with the power of the crest in my hands!

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:04.160
Faker, it's almost time...

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:10.210
I'll blow you all the way to the Parallel Universe with the very same power you desired!

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:13.960
Just wait... Just you wait!

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:21.890
Gramps, all I can do now is win in the Duel Carnival.

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:23.550
That's right, Yuma.

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:29.350
If you win the Carnival, Mr. Heartland will gladly do whatever you want.

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:35.570
Hey, Gramps. Who exactly is this Mr. Heartland guy?

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:43.280
What do you mean? Just as the name implies, he's Heartland's symbol and is quite popular with the kids.

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:45.660
I know all that.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:53.080
I know he's a symbol and that he's popular.

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:55.420
That's not what I mean!

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.710
If there's an outer there's an inner.

00:19:57.710 --> 00:20:00.130
Wherever you find light, you're bound to find a shadow.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:01.760
Well, that's the best way to describe it.

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:02.760
Shadow?

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:09.020
Mr. Heartland... You could say the one hiding behind him is the mastermind.

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:10.600
Mastermind?

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:12.440
What's that mean?

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:16.610
He's the one and only scientist called a genius in this decade.

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:18.360
Dr. Faker.

00:20:18.360 --> 00:20:20.030
And he's the mastermind?

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:22.610
He's a man surrounded by mystery.

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:27.240
He may be living right now or already dead.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:31.830
It's rumored that Dr. Faker was the one who created Heartland City.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:34.080
That Faker...

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:36.840
He was the last one to guide Kazuma.

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:42.840
Your dad and this man called Faker...

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:46.930
And if he's connected to Mr. Heartland, that means...

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:51.350
<i>If I step toward him, my father might be there.</i>

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:56.310
<i>In order to ensure it, I need to continue winning in the Duel Carnival.</i>

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:58.060
What?

00:20:58.060 --> 00:20:59.650
That boy from earlier?

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:03.780
Yes. Yuma Tsukumo holds the Original Number.

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:05.700
Yuma... Tsukumo?

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:06.620
Related to Kazuma Tsukumo?

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:07.820
Yes.

00:21:08.450 --> 00:21:09.330
It can't...

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:11.950
That can't be possible...

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:25.840
<i>That was the messenger from Astral World...</i>

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:33.020
Yuma Tsukumo...

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:42.820
If you're going to put that card in, you don't need the other one.

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:47.570
Shut up, will ya?! If I want it in, it's in! It's in!

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:51.120
Then you'd be better off replacing it with that Trap.

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:52.990
That one... Which one?

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:54.370
The one right there.

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:54.870
That.

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:01.710
Astral, let's win.

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:02.750
Naturally.

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:22.770
<i>Someone gave me some water.</i>

00:22:23.150 --> 00:22:28.700
<i>So I was able to paint a rainbow with ease.</i>

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:34.620
<i>I want to become someone perfect.</i>

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:37.660
<i>But it's very difficult.</i>

00:22:38.790 --> 00:22:41.250
<i>Even with me suffering,</i>

00:22:41.380 --> 00:22:45.340
<i>I can't seem to grasp victory.</i>

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:48.130
<i>I want to bloom!</i>

00:22:48.680 --> 00:22:52.600
<i>I must be having some kind of weird dream.</i>

00:22:52.600 --> 00:22:55.640
<i>But If I must fulfill this,</i>

00:22:56.140 --> 00:22:58.940
<i>Then I don't mind being laughed at for it.</i>

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:06.030
<i>Since it's because your limits are decided on your own.</i>

00:23:06.320 --> 00:23:09.070
<i>I'll show it, overcoming it to tomorrow.</i>

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:13.530
<i>Ah, I'm aiming for the big blue sky.</i>

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:15.490
<i>For all of its glory.</i>

00:23:15.490 --> 00:23:17.290
<i>The Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:22.670
<i>All of those countless flower petals</i>

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:25.710
<i>They came at the expense of</i>

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:29.300
<i>me being able to reach those heights.</i>

00:23:29.670 --> 00:23:33.720
<i>Ah, even though I lost my way today,</i>

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:35.560
<i>I still yearn for it.</i>

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:37.850
<i>That Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:42.020
Did you say Robin?!

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:44.270
<i>That</i> Robin is participating in the Duel Carnival?!

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:47.320
And he's up against Gauche of the Operation Committee!

00:23:47.320 --> 00:23:50.320
It's Dimensional ESPer Robin's friends!

00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:52.990
Such an awesome, awesome Duel!

00:23:52.990 --> 00:23:55.450
Both Robin and Gauche are intense!

00:23:55.450 --> 00:23:57.160
That Gauche's Monsters...

00:23:57.160 --> 00:23:59.370
No, I've seen that face before...

00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:01.250
Robin hasn't given up yet!

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:03.670
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal!

00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:06.670
"A Nemesis Shows Up Late! Robin VS Gauche"

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:08.670
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:24:10.550 --> 00:24:15.600
The WDC, lasting several days, is finally in its final day!

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:19.520
Just one more Heart Piece and my set is complete!

00:24:19.520 --> 00:24:23.940
I'm bringing it right to the tournament finals!
